# ── The photo archive's derivatives ──
# `npm run ingest:photos` writes a year of downscaled WebP here on its way to a
# Cloudflare Pages deploy. Thousands of image files per edition, rebuildable
# from the originals at any time, and deployed with wrangler rather than served
# from this repo — a git history carrying seventeen years of them would make
# every clone of this app enormous to no purpose.
build/

# ── Firebase service-account keys ──
# `npm run import:history -- --write` needs one, and the console downloads it as
# <project>-firebase-adminsdk-<hash>.json straight into whatever folder you point
# at. It is full read/write on the whole database with no rules in front of it —
# committing one is worse than a leaked password, because rotating it means
# revoking a key every deploy might depend on. None of these ever belong in git.
*firebase-adminsdk*.json
*serviceAccount*.json
*service-account*.json
*serviceAccountKey*.json

# ── Local Firebase project override (see .env.example) ──────────────────
# `*.local` above already covers .env.local; this catches a bare .env too.
# These files point a dev server at a scratch Firebase project, and a
# committed one would silently redirect every other machine's writes.
.env

# ── Store screenshots and the browser profile that takes them ──
# `npm run shots` writes both stores' image sets here, and keeps a signed-in
# Chromium profile so it does not have to ask every run. The images are
# regenerable from the app and the profile holds a real Google session — one
# is bulk, the other is a credential, and neither belongs in git.
store/screenshots/
.screenshot-profile/
# store/feature-graphic.png and store/play-icon-512.png ARE tracked — they are
# authored artwork rather than regenerable output, and rebuilding them needs
# Montserrat installed system-wide.
